WEBVTT

1
00:01:17.468 --> 00:01:18.499
THE SAFE WORKS?

2
00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:22.221
CLEAN SHEETS?

3
00:01:32.316 --> 00:01:33.976
SCENTED ROBES?

4
00:02:15.943 --> 00:02:17.354
Goodbye.

5
00:02:49.518 --> 00:02:52.353
- Did you forget something?
- No, thanks.

6
00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:06.993
Hello, may I help you?

7
00:03:18.964 --> 00:03:20.459
Mr. Manager...

8
00:03:20.716 --> 00:03:22.958
we have the mystery guest.

9
00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:24.797
Thank you.

10
00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:27.049
He'll be right here.

11
00:03:37.441 --> 00:03:42.602
I TRAVEL ALONE

12
00:05:23.088 --> 00:05:26.006
Will you show me
the spinach you meant?

13
00:05:33.348 --> 00:05:35.341
Looks perfect, what's wrong?

14
00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:37.261
We found snails.

15
00:05:37.352 --> 00:05:40.306
Great, that's proof
it's really organic.

16
00:05:40.397 --> 00:05:42.354
Why else would
our company be "Turf"?

17
00:05:42.441 --> 00:05:45.857
Our customers know this,
it's you I worry about.

18
00:05:49.823 --> 00:05:51.068
Hi.

19
00:05:51.283 --> 00:05:53.240
It's the Paris report,
will you give it to him?

20
00:05:53.452 --> 00:05:56.737
He's on a conference call,
but wants to see you, can you wait?

21
00:05:57.915 --> 00:06:01.864
No, I have so much to do,
I've been all over for two weeks.

22
00:06:04.671 --> 00:06:07.043
- You ripped them apart!
- With what they have you pay!

23
00:06:07.299 --> 00:06:08.674
I could have done much worse.

24
00:06:08.759 --> 00:06:11.166
Don't lose the enclosed photos,
they're worth seeing.

25
00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:17.510
I'm Andrea, the one in charge.

26
00:06:17.601 --> 00:06:20.934
They say there was a problem with
the last delivery, what happened?

27
00:06:21.021 --> 00:06:23.014
This cheese is inedible.

28
00:06:27.194 --> 00:06:29.519
Yes, you're right.

29
00:06:29.613 --> 00:06:32.863
Tell Carrozzoni we have
a problem with the cheese,

30
00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:35.357
then let's e-mail an apology
to our customers

31
00:06:35.452 --> 00:06:38.702
and with the next delivery
everyone gets complimentary cheese.

32
00:06:40.082 --> 00:06:42.489
Thank you for bothering
to come all the way here.

33
00:06:42.584 --> 00:06:46.913
I had to come this way
and thought I'd show it to you...

34
00:06:47.798 --> 00:06:50.668
- The rest of the box was delicious.
- Good.

35
00:06:52.386 --> 00:06:56.715
May I send you a complimentary box?
We have some wonderful pumpkins.

36
00:06:56.807 --> 00:06:58.467
Thank you.

37
00:06:58.684 --> 00:07:02.930
What box do you usually order?
The family-size or single?

38
00:07:08.902 --> 00:07:11.607
Simona is pregnant
and has resigned

39
00:07:11.696 --> 00:07:14.152
and Marzia is getting married.

40
00:07:14.241 --> 00:07:15.818
Marzia s getting married?

41
00:07:15.909 --> 00:07:19.325
- What about the girlfriend?
- They re getting married in Spain!

42
00:07:20.372 --> 00:07:23.492
She wants to quit working
to have time for the family.

43
00:07:23.708 --> 00:07:26.626
They re thinking of having a baby,
maybe of adopting one

44
00:07:26.711 --> 00:07:28.419
For Thursday.

45
00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:31.251
So they both gave notice
on the same day?

46
00:07:31.341 --> 00:07:32.883
Right,

47
00:07:32.968 --> 00:07:35.256
you're the only woman inspector left,

48
00:07:35.345 --> 00:07:37.254
you'll have
to take over their hotels.

49
00:07:37.347 --> 00:07:41.890
- More traveling, but more salary,
is that okay? - Sure.

50
00:07:41.977 --> 00:07:45.013
With women, it s always like this

51
00:07:45.105 --> 00:07:49.185
This is a job for singles
with no husbands, kids, girlfriends.

52
00:07:50.318 --> 00:07:52.525
Irene, are you there?
Are you following?

53
00:07:52.612 --> 00:07:56.990
I get it, I'm your ideal inspector
because I don't have a life.

54
00:07:57.075 --> 00:07:59.032
Goodbye.

55
00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:06.577
- Can I take a bath?
- Are you crazy?

56
00:08:06.793 --> 00:08:09.996
It's almost dinner time,
besides you know I'm against it.

57
00:08:10.088 --> 00:08:11.713
Against what?

58
00:08:11.798 --> 00:08:16.756
The tub, it takes too much water,
in 20 years there won't be any left.

59
00:08:16.845 --> 00:08:19.632
More reason to have one now!

60
00:08:19.848 --> 00:08:22.386
- You're smoking?
- No!

61
00:08:24.686 --> 00:08:26.844
I'll be dead in 20 years anyway.

62
00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:33.437
- I wasn't smoking.
- Sure...

63
00:08:41.953 --> 00:08:43.578
Please, taste it!

64
00:08:43.788 --> 00:08:45.864
- Delicious, did you make it?
- No.

65
00:08:46.124 --> 00:08:48.995
I got it from the Lebanese place,
the expensive one.

66
00:08:49.252 --> 00:08:50.877
The expensive one!

67
00:08:55.342 --> 00:08:57.418
It feels so good here!

68
00:08:58.303 --> 00:09:01.636
I should stay with you
when I get back from traveling.

69
00:09:05.101 --> 00:09:09.562
- Is it too much? Candles, roses...
- It's a bit over the top.

70
00:09:09.647 --> 00:09:12.352
- Better without?
- No, leave them.

71
00:09:12.442 --> 00:09:14.150
- You're sure?
- Yes.

72
00:09:15.904 --> 00:09:17.398
I'm off.

73
00:09:23.119 --> 00:09:24.827
Okay...

74
00:09:25.538 --> 00:09:27.447
- Where are you going now?
- The movies.

75
00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:29.248
- Who with?
- Me, myself and I.

76
00:09:29.334 --> 00:09:31.125
Nice little group!

77
00:09:31.628 --> 00:09:33.786
I can see going in the afternoon...
but isn't it a bit sad at night?

78
00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:35.623
Nighttime shows are for losers?

79
00:09:35.715 --> 00:09:39.629
As the day progresses,
a person's desperation increases?

80
00:09:39.719 --> 00:09:41.878
- Meaning?
- I'll explain later.

81
00:10:00.615 --> 00:10:03.071
- Please come in.
- Thank you.

82
00:10:03.159 --> 00:10:05.650
- I brought some wine.
- Thank you.

83
00:10:07.872 --> 00:10:09.580
Did you do the cooking?

84
00:10:10.667 --> 00:10:12.955
- Can I take your jacket?
- Yes, thank you.

85
00:10:29.310 --> 00:10:33.178
The work of a mystery guest
starts in the hall of a hotel

86
00:10:41.197 --> 00:10:44.780
Did the concierge look the guest
in the eyes when speaking?

87
00:10:44.993 --> 00:10:46.700
Did he smile?

88
00:10:48.246 --> 00:10:51.579
Did he use your name
when he welcomed you?

89
00:10:55.086 --> 00:10:58.206
Was the wait at the desk
less than two minutes?

90
00:11:00.925 --> 00:11:03.961
Was the desk clerk s uniform
clean and ironed?

91
00:11:04.762 --> 00:11:07.680
Were his shoes adequate standard?

92
00:11:09.183 --> 00:11:14.178
Does the hotel use a distinctive
scent in the halls and rooms?

93
00:11:23.573 --> 00:11:25.945
Were you given
a full explanation on how

94
00:11:26.159 --> 00:11:28.068
lights, the air conditioning, work?

95
00:11:31.038 --> 00:11:33.327
Was the temperature suitable?

96
00:11:49.348 --> 00:11:51.839
Did the steward wish the guest
a pleasant stay?

97
00:12:08.951 --> 00:12:10.908
FULL-LENGTH MIRROR?

98
00:12:19.211 --> 00:12:20.492
DVD PLAYER?

99
00:13:18.396 --> 00:13:22.144
- Do you need anything,
Mrs. Lorenzi? - No, thank you.

100
00:13:22.233 --> 00:13:24.309
You're not going skiing
on this beautiful day?

101
00:13:24.527 --> 00:13:26.899
Oh God, no, I hate snow.

102
00:13:28.322 --> 00:13:30.231
Are you here for work?

103
00:13:31.867 --> 00:13:33.445
No...

104
00:13:35.454 --> 00:13:37.079
A funeral.

105
00:13:38.374 --> 00:13:41.043
I'm sorry, please forgive me.

106
00:13:41.752 --> 00:13:43.496
Can I do anything for you?

107
00:13:45.422 --> 00:13:47.249
Maybe the music.

108
00:13:48.092 --> 00:13:50.843
Of course, I'll see to it right away.

109
00:13:56.684 --> 00:13:58.142
Come on!

110
00:13:58.686 --> 00:14:00.180
Good evening, we are...

111
00:14:00.396 --> 00:14:03.432
I'm sorry, the concert's started,
you can't go in now.

112
00:14:03.524 --> 00:14:08.316
- If we slide into a side seat?
- The doors are closed.

113
00:14:08.654 --> 00:14:09.899
Just imagine what they'll say!

114
00:14:09.989 --> 00:14:13.108
That's good, we know the concert
by heart, he practices everyday.

115
00:14:13.325 --> 00:14:15.863
But she said to get here on time!

116
00:14:16.996 --> 00:14:19.747
- Did you know it's dodecaphonic?
- It is?

117
00:14:21.667 --> 00:14:23.576
Okay... Ice cream?

118
00:14:25.004 --> 00:14:26.414
A nice ice cream cone.

119
00:14:31.468 --> 00:14:33.176
Here they are!

120
00:14:33.387 --> 00:14:35.261
Daddy, I'm so sorry.

121
00:14:35.347 --> 00:14:39.131
- We got held up.
- Don't tell me, traffic?

122
00:14:39.727 --> 00:14:43.807
Let's go have a pizza, I'm starving.

123
00:14:49.570 --> 00:14:52.440
Can I have a calzone
before the pizza?

124
00:14:52.698 --> 00:14:55.699
- I want the one with lots of cheese.
- Have what you like.

125
00:14:55.909 --> 00:14:57.949
Where did I leave it?

126
00:14:58.162 --> 00:15:01.163
- Shall we meet there?
- Wait a minute.

127
00:15:03.917 --> 00:15:08.081
- She did it again.
- She always parks on the crosswalk.

128
00:15:08.297 --> 00:15:10.171
Dammit...

129
00:15:12.718 --> 00:15:14.960
Where is the fucking car?
It was here!

130
00:15:17.431 --> 00:15:22.472
I'm in front of the Auditorium,
you towed my car.

131
00:15:23.103 --> 00:15:25.060
Wait, I'll ask my husband.
The plates?

132
00:15:25.147 --> 00:15:27.223
I don't remember.

133
00:15:27.316 --> 00:15:30.103
- Who's she talking to?
- To the guys that tow cars.

134
00:15:30.319 --> 00:15:33.070
She's got the number
stored on her phone.

135
00:15:33.238 --> 00:15:35.397
You took just mine, then that's it.

136
00:16:25.582 --> 00:16:27.076
I'm starving.

137
00:16:27.292 --> 00:16:29.914
- Me too.
- Be patient.

138
00:16:30.003 --> 00:16:32.043
I'll call a taxi again.

139
00:16:32.130 --> 00:16:34.704
Another one?
No, we all stay here together.

140
00:16:35.050 --> 00:16:37.802
No more taxis,
they mustn't get into the habit.

141
00:16:38.011 --> 00:16:40.419
- They've taken two this evening.
- You count the cabs?

142
00:16:40.514 --> 00:16:43.087
Of course, they're regular kids,
not Paris Hilton!

143
00:16:43.183 --> 00:16:46.054
Paris Hilton?
Restaurants close at 11.

144
00:16:46.144 --> 00:16:48.931
They'll wait,
they need to learn solidarity,

145
00:16:49.147 --> 00:16:51.436
meaning we'll have
a nice falafel all together,

146
00:16:51.650 --> 00:16:54.567
they're open till late. What is it?

147
00:16:54.778 --> 00:16:56.569
- No...
- Felafel...

148
00:16:56.655 --> 00:16:59.360
It seems they finally found it.

149
00:16:59.574 --> 00:17:02.112
- Let's go or I'll faint away.
- Let's go!

150
00:17:02.202 --> 00:17:04.574
You have the keys.

151
00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:08.617
Have you got them?

152
00:17:11.545 --> 00:17:13.122
- Have you got them or not?
- Yes!

153
00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:24.385
Good morning, Mrs Lorenzi,
it s 8 a m

154
00:17:24.599 --> 00:17:26.925
and the outside temperature
is 18 degrees celsius

155
00:17:47.664 --> 00:17:49.740
Did you bring some money?

156
00:17:50.333 --> 00:17:52.409
Do we have to pay to get in?

157
00:17:52.627 --> 00:17:54.703
I don't think so.

158
00:17:54.921 --> 00:17:57.128
Maybe you'd better go ask downstairs.

159
00:17:58.925 --> 00:18:01.879
The spa is free of charge
for all hotel guests.

160
00:18:01.970 --> 00:18:05.090
- Thank you.
- Not at all, don't mention it.

161
00:18:22.699 --> 00:18:24.988
Good morning, I'll bring
the menu right away.

162
00:18:25.243 --> 00:18:27.319
- Are you alone?
- Yes.

163
00:19:11.915 --> 00:19:14.619
Hello,
I'd like to order a club sandwich,

164
00:19:14.834 --> 00:19:16.293
a Thai soup

165
00:19:16.503 --> 00:19:19.207
and a berry mixture with mango.

166
00:19:19.464 --> 00:19:22.749
No mango.
Then an orange Bavarian cream

167
00:19:22.967 --> 00:19:24.841
and a Franciacorta to drink.

168
00:19:58.545 --> 00:20:00.621
What happened?

169
00:20:02.590 --> 00:20:04.250
You don't mind if I stay?

170
00:20:04.467 --> 00:20:07.801
No, I'm glad, but what's wrong?
You put me in a state.

171
00:20:09.055 --> 00:20:11.511
I didn't want to tell you
on the phone, sorry.

172
00:20:11.599 --> 00:20:14.137
- Oh God, then it's serious.
- Can I smoke here?

173
00:20:14.227 --> 00:20:17.263
We'll get arrested here,
we can go to the terrace.

174
00:20:17.355 --> 00:20:19.348
Great, you started again?

175
00:20:21.859 --> 00:20:25.478
- Is she the one
I passed in the elevator? - Yes.

176
00:20:25.571 --> 00:20:27.694
What did you tell her?

177
00:20:27.782 --> 00:20:31.447
I don't want
to have a child with a stranger.

178
00:20:31.536 --> 00:20:33.742
She's forcing it on me.

179
00:20:33.955 --> 00:20:36.031
Fuck it, it's unfair!

180
00:20:36.249 --> 00:20:40.460
Now it feels that way, but
at that moment... sorry to say so.

181
00:20:40.545 --> 00:20:42.584
She said she'll have
the baby anyway,

182
00:20:42.797 --> 00:20:45.205
because given her age,
it's crazy not to,

183
00:20:45.425 --> 00:20:46.835
it's her decision, and,

184
00:20:47.051 --> 00:20:50.171
if I don't want to be the father,
she won't expect anything from me.

185
00:20:50.263 --> 00:20:52.172
She said that?

186
00:20:56.352 --> 00:20:57.763
Hang on.

187
00:21:03.192 --> 00:21:05.268
Hello, Mrs. Lorenzi.

188
00:21:15.246 --> 00:21:17.155
Please sign.

189
00:21:31.429 --> 00:21:33.137
Thank you, goodbye.

190
00:21:41.856 --> 00:21:45.640
- What did he do wrong?
- He didn't pour me a glass.

191
00:21:52.825 --> 00:21:55.316
You know what worries me the most?

192
00:21:55.536 --> 00:21:57.196
What are you doing?

193
00:21:59.707 --> 00:22:01.996
The wine is two degrees too warm.

194
00:22:07.215 --> 00:22:11.046
The soup should be at least 40
and it's not.

195
00:22:11.260 --> 00:22:12.920
What a tragedy!

196
00:22:13.137 --> 00:22:17.514
I know, but these are the kinds
of problems I'm paid to deal with.

197
00:22:18.309 --> 00:22:19.589
Done, tell me.

198
00:22:20.603 --> 00:22:23.355
What troubles me the most is that...

199
00:22:23.564 --> 00:22:25.604
Have a little soup.

200
00:22:25.816 --> 00:22:30.194
- Not now, will you just listen
to me. - Because it was hot, sorry.

201
00:22:58.099 --> 00:23:00.175
What are you writing?

202
00:23:00.267 --> 00:23:02.094
- My novel.
- Your novel?

203
00:23:02.186 --> 00:23:04.392
- Didn't I tell you?
- No.

204
00:23:06.107 --> 00:23:08.183
- Can I read a few lines to you?
- Yes.

205
00:23:08.401 --> 00:23:11.686
It's the first draft,
I'm a bit intimidated.

206
00:23:13.280 --> 00:23:17.907
At 1:45 p.m. I asked the concierge
for the nearest pharmacy.

207
00:23:17.993 --> 00:23:20.615
Not only did he not
send someone to get

208
00:23:20.704 --> 00:23:22.863
what I needed,

209
00:23:22.957 --> 00:23:25.661
but he indicated the pharmacy to me

210
00:23:25.751 --> 00:23:27.708
without worrying that I might...

211
00:23:27.795 --> 00:23:30.630
I see, it's not really my taste.

212
00:23:30.714 --> 00:23:33.585
Wait, there's
a dramatic turn of events!

213
00:23:34.426 --> 00:23:37.511
Do you have to write this novel
every time?

214
00:23:37.721 --> 00:23:39.797
The plot's always the same.

215
00:23:57.324 --> 00:23:59.862
- Eggs and American coffee.
- Yes, please.

216
00:24:01.662 --> 00:24:04.367
Sorry, there's a gentleman today too.

217
00:24:04.623 --> 00:24:06.248
I'm sorry, I hadn't noticed.

218
00:24:06.458 --> 00:24:08.831
- Would you like something?
- A large coffee.

219
00:24:09.878 --> 00:24:11.622
I ordered eggs and bacon for you.

220
00:24:11.839 --> 00:24:13.915
I don't eat savory things
at breakfast.

221
00:24:14.133 --> 00:24:18.296
Please, help me, I've put on
two kilos since I got here.

222
00:24:18.554 --> 00:24:21.471
- Find yourself an assistant.
- I did!

223
00:24:29.565 --> 00:24:31.225
Stress.

224
00:24:31.859 --> 00:24:34.776
- What's her name?
- Fabiana.

225
00:24:34.987 --> 00:24:37.608
- Fabiana what?
- Cantoni.

226
00:24:38.240 --> 00:24:40.945
And what does Fabiana Cantoni do?

227
00:24:41.160 --> 00:24:45.786
She has a place that's half
picture gallery, half coffee bar.

228
00:24:52.755 --> 00:24:55.459
And if this had happened
when we were together?

229
00:24:55.966 --> 00:24:58.671
Would you have had a child with me?

230
00:24:59.470 --> 00:25:02.139
- How 's that fit here now?
- It fits.

231
00:25:03.682 --> 00:25:05.474
Answer me.

232
00:25:06.769 --> 00:25:09.141
- No, I don't think so.
- No?

233
00:25:10.522 --> 00:25:11.767
Why not?

234
00:25:11.857 --> 00:25:14.774
I don't know,
I've never felt the need,

235
00:25:14.860 --> 00:25:17.481
it's not mandatory, you know!

236
00:25:17.571 --> 00:25:19.528
If we'd had one, he'd be 15.

237
00:25:19.740 --> 00:25:21.282
Good thing we didn't!

238
00:25:23.869 --> 00:25:25.826
I'm late, I have to go.

239
00:25:28.499 --> 00:25:30.954
- We'll be in touch later.
- Yes, I'll call you.

240
00:25:31.543 --> 00:25:33.619
It made me feel better
talking to you.

241
00:25:42.554 --> 00:25:45.674
- Has the gentleman already left?
- Yes, he was in a rush.

242
00:25:45.891 --> 00:25:47.551
Forgive me for not coming promptly,

243
00:25:47.768 --> 00:25:50.093
it's mayhem here today.

244
00:25:50.187 --> 00:25:53.390
Apparently there's a mystery guest,

245
00:25:54.274 --> 00:25:58.189
an incognito inspector,
one who checks quality standards,

246
00:25:58.445 --> 00:26:00.687
and we're all in quite a state.

247
00:26:00.989 --> 00:26:02.483
He's behind you.

248
00:26:10.415 --> 00:26:14.793
Eggs Benedict are poached eggs
topped with Hollandaise sauce

249
00:26:15.629 --> 00:26:17.503
served with bacon.

250
00:26:17.756 --> 00:26:19.796
When taking the order, is the waiter

251
00:26:20.008 --> 00:26:21.882
smiling and pleasant?

252
00:26:22.094 --> 00:26:23.469
What's Hollandaise sauce?

253
00:26:23.553 --> 00:26:26.258
A sauce made with egg yolks
and butter, Madam.

254
00:26:26.473 --> 00:26:30.008
Did he reply readily and courteously
to any question about the menu?

255
00:26:30.227 --> 00:26:31.887
I don't know...

256
00:26:32.104 --> 00:26:35.223
I have other tables to serve,
I'll be back in a moment.

257
00:26:51.665 --> 00:26:56.126
A moment of distraction or edginess
on the part of the waiter

258
00:26:56.336 --> 00:26:58.661
cannot invalidate a score.

259
00:26:58.880 --> 00:27:01.834
I'd kept an eye on two guests
for three days

260
00:27:01.925 --> 00:27:03.918
and they were constantly neglected.

261
00:27:04.010 --> 00:27:07.925
You intend to lower our score
for this small incident?

262
00:27:08.014 --> 00:27:10.090
It might be small for you,
Mr. Manager.

263
00:27:10.308 --> 00:27:14.057
I remind you
of our criteria for 5-stars:

264
00:27:14.271 --> 00:27:16.429
It is a hotel that's
supposed to be extraordinary,

265
00:27:16.648 --> 00:27:19.269
by offering a unique experience
through impeccable service.

266
00:27:19.359 --> 00:27:22.313
The staff must be intuitive,
enthusiastic, attentive

267
00:27:22.404 --> 00:27:24.729
providing a service
that exceeds the expectations.

268
00:27:25.365 --> 00:27:28.319
To grumble at a guest because he
doesn't know what Eggs Benedict are

269
00:27:28.535 --> 00:27:30.693
is not intuitive,
nor enthusiastic, nor attentive.

270
00:27:30.996 --> 00:27:35.408
That couple must receive the same
treatment as the other guests,

271
00:27:35.500 --> 00:27:37.908
even if it's their first time
at a 5-star hotel,

272
00:27:38.003 --> 00:27:42.380
even if their relatives
gave them this honeymoon,

273
00:27:42.465 --> 00:27:45.170
even if they wear beach robes
to the pool and aren't chic.

274
00:27:53.018 --> 00:27:54.346
Can I give you a hand?

275
00:27:54.603 --> 00:27:58.221
Yes, when you're done, put the
cigarette out and close the window.

276
00:27:58.815 --> 00:28:01.104
I'm coming, it's out.

277
00:28:05.155 --> 00:28:06.614
What can I do?

278
00:28:06.823 --> 00:28:10.773
Auntie, help us clean these,
they're all muddy.

279
00:28:10.994 --> 00:28:14.778
Isn't packaged lettuce better,
like from the supermarket?

280
00:28:14.873 --> 00:28:19.535
Sure, but it doesn't have
the same nutrition value...

281
00:28:19.628 --> 00:28:22.545
I mean it's like eating paper,
do you like paper?

282
00:28:22.797 --> 00:28:26.380
Andrea's veggies were picked
12 hours ago, they're fresher.

283
00:28:26.635 --> 00:28:29.090
I always buy packaged lettuce.

284
00:28:29.304 --> 00:28:33.681
What a pain! I have to talk
to Federica on Skype.

285
00:28:33.767 --> 00:28:35.973
I thought we'd agreed.

286
00:28:36.061 --> 00:28:38.765
Let them go, we can do it.

287
00:28:39.981 --> 00:28:41.012
Go on.

288
00:28:44.611 --> 00:28:46.271
They always get their way.

289
00:28:46.488 --> 00:28:48.943
I wanted to do something
all together.

290
00:28:49.157 --> 00:28:51.695
What fun, cleaning spinach!

291
00:28:51.910 --> 00:28:55.860
Everyone in this house is always
either on a computer or on the phone.

292
00:28:56.081 --> 00:29:00.659
Tommaso has a thing with that game,
"The Farm", do you know it?

293
00:29:00.752 --> 00:29:02.543
No, what is it?

294
00:29:02.754 --> 00:29:04.830
You buy a farm,

295
00:29:05.090 --> 00:29:08.708
you can plant vegetables:
Carrots, potatoes.

296
00:29:08.802 --> 00:29:12.751
You can also buy animals:
Pigs, cows, rabbits

297
00:29:12.972 --> 00:29:15.261
and you can trade them.

298
00:29:15.475 --> 00:29:17.966
You'll get a ton of potatoes
for a cow,

299
00:29:18.186 --> 00:29:21.306
a ton of grain for a rabbit.

300
00:29:22.107 --> 00:29:24.644
But it's all virtual reality.

301
00:29:25.819 --> 00:29:28.736
They're not real cows, horses,

302
00:29:28.947 --> 00:29:30.145
it's all pretend animals.

303
00:29:30.365 --> 00:29:32.690
I don't get it.

304
00:29:33.201 --> 00:29:34.992
Me neither.

305
00:29:36.496 --> 00:29:40.031
Not the rabbits!
They're taking my rabbits away.

306
00:29:40.250 --> 00:29:44.199
He's glued to that screen all day,
harvesting, planting,

307
00:29:44.420 --> 00:29:46.543
buying and trading animals.

308
00:29:46.756 --> 00:29:50.505
There are 4 million people
who play this game.

309
00:29:50.593 --> 00:29:52.918
- How 's his work going?
- Fine.

310
00:29:53.555 --> 00:29:57.932
I mean, today a musician's pay
is half what a plumber makes.

311
00:29:58.518 --> 00:30:01.887
Anyway, we know the place of culture
in this country, don't we?

312
00:30:02.105 --> 00:30:05.355
Actually, I'm worried
about your situation.

313
00:30:05.441 --> 00:30:07.897
M e? Ow come?

314
00:30:08.111 --> 00:30:09.984
They have you pretend to be rich

315
00:30:10.196 --> 00:30:12.355
and then give you
a skilled worker's wage.

316
00:30:12.448 --> 00:30:16.778
My bills are paid, I live in luxury
hotels, it could be worse.

317
00:30:16.995 --> 00:30:18.240
Sure,

318
00:30:18.454 --> 00:30:21.372
but you don't have a family,
kids, a husband,

319
00:30:21.582 --> 00:30:23.659
not even a steady job.

320
00:30:23.918 --> 00:30:26.753
I wonder: What will Irene do
twenty years from now?

321
00:30:26.838 --> 00:30:28.914
Who'll take care of her?

322
00:30:30.133 --> 00:30:31.710
You.

323
00:30:31.801 --> 00:30:34.553
Okay, but what if I die first?

324
00:30:35.805 --> 00:30:36.920
Them.

325
00:30:37.432 --> 00:30:39.590
Your beloved nieces!

326
00:30:39.684 --> 00:30:43.978
If you want to count on them,
you'll have to invest more time.

327
00:30:44.063 --> 00:30:47.064
You haven't built a real intimacy,
sorry to tell you.

328
00:30:47.316 --> 00:30:48.692
What are you saying?

329
00:30:48.901 --> 00:30:52.816
Building a deep relationship
takes much more commitment.

330
00:30:52.905 --> 00:30:55.823
- You're so aggressive!
- Me?

331
00:30:55.908 --> 00:31:00.321
I'm worried, you're not a spring
chicken and you're alone.

332
00:31:00.413 --> 00:31:02.738
You should worry about your husband,

333
00:31:02.957 --> 00:31:05.199
and the time he spends
trading chickens.

334
00:32:59.865 --> 00:33:02.535
I can see you again next month,

335
00:33:02.785 --> 00:33:06.368
in the meantime you can start
the prenatal yoga course here.

336
00:33:07.289 --> 00:33:09.578
Take a look at the leaflet
on water birth,

337
00:33:09.834 --> 00:33:12.503
so that you and your husband
can think it over.

338
00:33:13.379 --> 00:33:15.039
Of course.

339
00:33:43.284 --> 00:33:46.487
- Want a lift?
- No, thanks, I have a car.

340
00:33:46.787 --> 00:33:49.907
Let me know when you make
the next appointment.

341
00:33:50.499 --> 00:33:52.788
Andrea, there's no need.

342
00:33:53.043 --> 00:33:54.917
I told you I want to come.

343
00:33:56.338 --> 00:33:58.295
As you like.

344
00:34:36.128 --> 00:34:39.462
When will she get here?
It's almost 9, I'm hungry.

345
00:34:39.673 --> 00:34:42.081
She's on her way, be patient.

346
00:34:42.301 --> 00:34:46.001
Call her, maybe she's right outside,
so we can start the pasta.

347
00:34:50.017 --> 00:34:53.220
I told her at 8:30,
she's not even 15 minutes late.

348
00:35:03.155 --> 00:35:05.824
- Where is she?
- She must have forgotten.

349
00:35:10.704 --> 00:35:13.076
Come on, put the pasta in.

350
00:36:20.983 --> 00:36:22.393
Vacation or work?

351
00:36:22.484 --> 00:36:23.480
Work.

352
00:36:23.568 --> 00:36:25.312
Let's see...

353
00:36:26.780 --> 00:36:28.440
Photographer?

354
00:36:28.782 --> 00:36:30.691
Writer?

355
00:36:31.368 --> 00:36:33.111
Are you in politics?

356
00:36:33.412 --> 00:36:35.369
Lmport-export of Berber carpets.

357
00:36:36.498 --> 00:36:37.743
I give up.

358
00:36:39.793 --> 00:36:41.073
Do you have to leave?

359
00:36:43.005 --> 00:36:45.756
I'm in the tiles business.

360
00:36:49.886 --> 00:36:51.131
Tiles?

361
00:36:51.221 --> 00:36:52.501
Yes, handcrafted tiles.

362
00:36:53.015 --> 00:36:58.768
I buy them wholesale from a company
specializing in renovation.

363
00:37:00.480 --> 00:37:03.054
I have to do some at my house.

364
00:37:03.358 --> 00:37:04.769
You could help me

365
00:37:04.860 --> 00:37:06.402
choose the flooring for the patio.

366
00:37:07.112 --> 00:37:08.736
A patio?

367
00:37:12.492 --> 00:37:14.532
Terracotta,

368
00:37:14.619 --> 00:37:16.363
it's easy.

369
00:37:16.705 --> 00:37:17.487
Personally...

370
00:37:18.373 --> 00:37:19.832
personally...

371
00:37:19.916 --> 00:37:23.202
personally I'd avoid bright colors

372
00:37:24.087 --> 00:37:25.036
with the exception of blue,

373
00:37:25.130 --> 00:37:26.957
it's resistant to the elements.

374
00:37:27.924 --> 00:37:30.332
Today there are special glues

375
00:37:30.427 --> 00:37:32.419
to lay any type

376
00:37:32.512 --> 00:37:33.923
of outside flooring,

377
00:37:34.014 --> 00:37:36.302
but without the same results.

378
00:37:38.602 --> 00:37:40.060
Back to the patio,

379
00:37:40.145 --> 00:37:42.054
you should choose light colors.

380
00:37:43.106 --> 00:37:46.024
The permeability of terracotta
is overestimated.

381
00:37:53.200 --> 00:37:56.117
I'm not sure I believe this story.

382
00:37:57.537 --> 00:37:59.446
I think, there's something else.

383
00:37:59.748 --> 00:38:03.448
That means there's a secret.

384
00:38:03.752 --> 00:38:04.997
Of course.

385
00:38:05.545 --> 00:38:07.454
Could you be a spy?

386
00:38:08.340 --> 00:38:10.048
A sort of.

387
00:38:30.737 --> 00:38:32.065
Mine's there.

388
00:38:33.365 --> 00:38:34.610
And mine's there.

389
00:38:40.664 --> 00:38:42.740
You're a very beautiful woman,

390
00:38:44.459 --> 00:38:47.294
but I'm very married, very faithful.

391
00:38:49.255 --> 00:38:50.500
M e too

392
00:38:51.299 --> 00:38:52.544
Good night.

393
00:39:08.274 --> 00:39:12.272
Would you say the hotel is right for
younger people or the more mature?

394
00:39:15.031 --> 00:39:18.566
Is it for families,
couples or singles?

395
00:39:39.013 --> 00:39:40.556
May I help you?

396
00:39:40.765 --> 00:39:42.924
I'd like to speak to the manager.

397
00:39:46.271 --> 00:39:48.726
Heavens... I'll get him right away.

398
00:39:49.065 --> 00:39:51.271
Please take the lady to the manager.

399
00:39:51.651 --> 00:39:52.647
Of course.

400
00:40:00.952 --> 00:40:04.072
A small problem
with the tiles in my room.

401
00:40:09.460 --> 00:40:12.212
Do you think smoke
is bad for vegetables?

402
00:40:12.422 --> 00:40:14.498
It certainly does no good.

403
00:40:14.716 --> 00:40:18.879
I have to be reliable, if I promise
quality, I must guarantee it.

404
00:40:19.387 --> 00:40:21.261
And here's me telling you...

405
00:40:21.889 --> 00:40:24.096
Actually, we do very similar work.

406
00:40:24.183 --> 00:40:27.635
Yes, but I'm always here
and you're a world away.

407
00:40:30.064 --> 00:40:32.140
I've got 300,000 free miles,

408
00:40:32.400 --> 00:40:35.733
why don't we go to Brazil
after the summer?

409
00:40:36.112 --> 00:40:39.861
Five-star hotels, all expenses paid,
wonderful... like the idea?

410
00:40:40.074 --> 00:40:42.779
The baby's due at the end of summer.

411
00:40:43.786 --> 00:40:45.826
That's right.

412
00:40:51.169 --> 00:40:53.660
- Come on, let's go to the movies.
- Okay, I'm done.

413
00:40:54.547 --> 00:40:56.504
I'll turn this off...

414
00:40:57.008 --> 00:41:00.293
Done, I'll put the cart
in the fridge and I'm finished.

415
00:41:00.553 --> 00:41:03.044
- What?
- I'll put the cart in the fridge.

416
00:41:04.098 --> 00:41:06.387
Please turn off the lights?

417
00:41:48.434 --> 00:41:50.890
Hello, if you need anything,
just ask.

418
00:41:51.103 --> 00:41:53.855
- No, thank you, I'm just looking.
- Take your time.

419
00:42:08.120 --> 00:42:11.038
That's right, for the 15th and 16th.

420
00:42:11.958 --> 00:42:16.121
There are three of us, so I'll need
a suite or two adjoining rooms.

421
00:42:18.464 --> 00:42:21.584
Excellent, Mrs. Lorenzi,
two adjoining rooms.

422
00:42:21.801 --> 00:42:23.710
For the 15th and the 16th

423
00:42:51.122 --> 00:42:53.909
Lift the bedcover
and look at the sheet,

424
00:42:54.125 --> 00:42:56.413
are there stains or whatnot?

425
00:42:56.627 --> 00:42:58.916
Do the sheets have a nice scent?

426
00:42:59.755 --> 00:43:02.922
- Everything's fine here, Auntie.
- Here too.

427
00:43:03.008 --> 00:43:04.800
They're doing alright.

428
00:43:06.303 --> 00:43:09.388
Girls, remember
we're on a secret mission,

429
00:43:09.473 --> 00:43:11.382
I'm your mother.

430
00:43:14.812 --> 00:43:17.729
Go towards Fasano,
then take the exit for Alberobello.

431
00:43:17.940 --> 00:43:19.399
How many kilometers?

432
00:43:19.650 --> 00:43:22.106
6-7 to get to Fasano

433
00:43:22.319 --> 00:43:24.146
and another 3...
about twenty kilometers.

434
00:43:24.238 --> 00:43:26.480
Mom!

435
00:43:27.283 --> 00:43:29.952
Ma'am, your girls are calling you.

436
00:43:30.744 --> 00:43:31.989
Of course.

437
00:43:32.204 --> 00:43:33.948
- Irene!
- Right here.

438
00:43:36.083 --> 00:43:37.791
Well?

439
00:43:41.672 --> 00:43:44.626
Good, girls! Let's go!

440
00:44:14.371 --> 00:44:16.447
We finished, Auntie.

441
00:44:17.082 --> 00:44:18.742
I'll be right there.

442
00:44:19.877 --> 00:44:21.953
No, not the toilet paper, no!

443
00:44:30.554 --> 00:44:32.843
Oh no, what is this?

444
00:44:33.474 --> 00:44:35.182
What's all this mess?
Are you crazy?

445
00:44:35.434 --> 00:44:39.218
One thing is our inspection,
another is being ill-behaved.

446
00:44:39.313 --> 00:44:42.812
Put everything back
the way you found it, right now!

447
00:44:52.785 --> 00:44:55.786
- When's your rehearsal tomorrow?
- At 4.

448
00:44:58.832 --> 00:45:00.908
Will you take Eleonora to the pool?

449
00:45:01.126 --> 00:45:03.000
Sure, no problem.

450
00:45:14.640 --> 00:45:16.679
- What is it?
- Nothing.

451
00:45:16.767 --> 00:45:18.344
Why are you looking at me like that?

452
00:45:18.435 --> 00:45:21.140
How?
I'm not looking at you in any way.

453
00:45:26.652 --> 00:45:28.110
Tommaso?

454
00:45:29.988 --> 00:45:31.399
What?

455
00:45:31.657 --> 00:45:35.489
- Don't you ever think about it?
- What?

456
00:45:36.537 --> 00:45:38.197
The fact that...

457
00:45:39.873 --> 00:45:41.949
we don't have sex anymore?

458
00:45:47.798 --> 00:45:51.333
I'd like to know
if this is a transitory phase

459
00:45:51.552 --> 00:45:54.967
or whether there's no turning back,
what do you say?

460
00:45:56.056 --> 00:45:59.176
I don't know, does it worry you?

461
00:45:59.393 --> 00:46:01.053
A little.

462
00:46:01.270 --> 00:46:02.930
Sorry, but don't you miss it?

463
00:46:03.021 --> 00:46:05.061
- No.
- No?

464
00:46:05.148 --> 00:46:07.936
I mean yes, but I'm okay with it.

465
00:46:09.695 --> 00:46:12.268
Then if you're okay with it...

466
00:46:12.364 --> 00:46:15.281
Clearly,
I do think about it sometimes,

467
00:46:15.367 --> 00:46:17.276
but not obsessively.

468
00:46:17.369 --> 00:46:20.572
It's not like, every night
I'm thinking... you know?

469
00:46:24.626 --> 00:46:27.331
Don't you ever have a sexual dream?

470
00:46:28.588 --> 00:46:31.293
What?
I don't know, I don't remember...

471
00:46:31.508 --> 00:46:34.628
- It's normal.
- Yes, I might have had one...

472
00:46:36.471 --> 00:46:38.345
And you?

473
00:46:38.557 --> 00:46:42.886
I do, very often recently,
but always with someone different.

474
00:46:42.978 --> 00:46:46.014
With absurd people,
that I don't even like in real life.

475
00:46:46.106 --> 00:46:48.182
Like who, for example?

476
00:46:48.400 --> 00:46:50.476
- Do you really want me to tell you?
- Yes.

477
00:46:51.319 --> 00:46:53.893
- With your accountant.
- Franconi?

478
00:46:54.114 --> 00:46:57.031
- Come on, he's an ogre!
- Really.

479
00:46:57.325 --> 00:46:59.235
And you?

480
00:47:01.079 --> 00:47:04.614
Come on, they're just fantasies,
I told you mine.

481
00:47:05.792 --> 00:47:09.078
- Come on, you have them.
- Once with...

482
00:47:09.171 --> 00:47:12.088
with Antonella, the flautist,
the redhead.

483
00:47:12.299 --> 00:47:14.375
The fat one? No!

484
00:47:25.812 --> 00:47:26.927
Good Lord...

485
00:47:35.363 --> 00:47:38.483
I think we should talk to someone.

486
00:47:42.746 --> 00:47:44.620
Come on, cut it out.

487
00:47:46.208 --> 00:47:48.284
I don't like it here anymore.

488
00:47:49.169 --> 00:47:51.660
- Please.
- Stop it!

489
00:47:53.215 --> 00:47:55.291
You always spoil everything.

490
00:47:59.429 --> 00:48:02.928
- What happened?
- Nothing happened.

491
00:48:03.016 --> 00:48:06.136
I don't like staying here,
lwant to go home.

492
00:48:07.395 --> 00:48:09.933
Don't listen to her,
she's a baby, she'll stop.

493
00:48:12.233 --> 00:48:15.151
I'm sorry, I raised my voice earlier,
I didn't mean to...

494
00:48:15.362 --> 00:48:18.197
Don't make it a tragedy, come on.

495
00:48:18.281 --> 00:48:20.951
I want Mommy.

496
00:48:21.159 --> 00:48:24.777
It's just for tonight,
we'll go home tomorrow.

497
00:48:24.871 --> 00:48:26.698
- Alright?
- Okay.

498
00:48:33.421 --> 00:48:34.999
Come on...

499
00:49:40.822 --> 00:49:42.696
Thank you. Did they behave?

500
00:50:10.184 --> 00:50:11.216
Well?

501
00:50:11.436 --> 00:50:14.140
There's a tub,
but you don't use one anyway.

502
00:50:14.355 --> 00:50:17.440
- Besides that?
- It's huge.

503
00:50:17.525 --> 00:50:19.814
It has just one more room than mine.

504
00:50:20.528 --> 00:50:22.604
But why all this rush?

505
00:50:22.864 --> 00:50:24.940
I told you, my contract's up

506
00:50:25.825 --> 00:50:28.743
and I'd be closer to Fabiana
for when the baby comes.

507
00:50:28.953 --> 00:50:32.120
- Fabiana lives around here?
- Five minutes away.

508
00:50:34.417 --> 00:50:36.955
Well, can you see me in here?

509
00:50:37.045 --> 00:50:40.295
If you follow me,
I'll show you the bedroom.

510
00:50:40.381 --> 00:50:42.125
This way.

511
00:50:45.845 --> 00:50:47.672
As you see,

512
00:50:47.930 --> 00:50:50.006
it will hold a very large wardrobe

513
00:50:50.224 --> 00:50:54.388
and the night area's perfect,
it's near your bathroom...

514
00:50:54.604 --> 00:50:58.352
No, I'm a just a friend,
we don't live together.

515
00:50:58.441 --> 00:51:00.315
She's just here
to give me her opinion.

516
00:51:00.401 --> 00:51:03.023
Sorry, I misunderstood.

517
00:51:04.363 --> 00:51:06.652
Well? What do you think?

518
00:51:07.283 --> 00:51:09.359
I don't know...

519
00:51:11.037 --> 00:51:15.200
The kitchen is tiny,
there's no counter space.

520
00:51:15.416 --> 00:51:18.334
Since you're always cooking,
I wouldn't say it's ideal.

521
00:51:18.544 --> 00:51:21.878
This room has a horrible view,
the other's very small,

522
00:51:22.089 --> 00:51:24.082
I just find it horribly depressing.

523
00:51:24.175 --> 00:51:26.666
But you decide,
I don't want to influence you.

524
00:51:26.761 --> 00:51:28.800
You're not very encouraging though.

525
00:51:28.888 --> 00:51:33.051
It's my opinion, do as you like,
you're the one who has to live here.

526
00:51:34.101 --> 00:51:36.592
The doors, I'd say, are nice.

527
00:51:38.397 --> 00:51:41.102
Can't you find
an early morning flight?

528
00:51:43.903 --> 00:51:46.820
No, I'll hang on,
so we can wrap it up.

529
00:51:49.784 --> 00:51:52.904
I want to get there
in the early morning for breakfast.

530
00:51:54.580 --> 00:51:56.656
Not even the other airport?

531
00:52:00.086 --> 00:52:02.162
No, it's not you!

532
00:52:04.757 --> 00:52:07.462
Look again, check everything.

533
00:52:12.139 --> 00:52:14.215
It's for a formal event,

534
00:52:14.433 --> 00:52:16.889
I don't want to wear
the usual black slacks!

535
00:52:17.144 --> 00:52:20.763
7 is perfect, what time do I arrive?

536
00:52:20.856 --> 00:52:22.979
Wonderful, book that one, thanks.

537
00:52:23.067 --> 00:52:25.558
Yes, send me everything via e-mail.

538
00:52:26.821 --> 00:52:29.525
- Try this.
- No, I want to be more...

539
00:52:29.740 --> 00:52:31.816
Bye, see you soon.

540
00:52:32.034 --> 00:52:34.359
More what? Try this!

541
00:52:34.453 --> 00:52:37.703
- This looks terrible on you.
- That bad?

542
00:52:38.958 --> 00:52:41.081
Silvia, come on!

543
00:52:45.172 --> 00:52:48.126
I can't come to dinner this evening,

544
00:52:48.342 --> 00:52:50.667
I have to pack,
I leave tomorrow morning early.

545
00:52:50.761 --> 00:52:53.964
What did you mean
the other dress wasn't me?

546
00:52:54.890 --> 00:52:58.176
That you did well to buy
the brown one, it suits you better.

547
00:52:58.269 --> 00:53:01.435
You didn't say it didn't look good
on me, but that it wasn't me.

548
00:53:01.981 --> 00:53:03.641
Who do you think I am?

549
00:53:03.858 --> 00:53:06.775
You're a woman
who'd never wear that type of dress,

550
00:53:06.986 --> 00:53:09.477
in fact, I've never seen one
like it in your closet.

551
00:53:09.697 --> 00:53:11.939
- You ran a red light.
- I know.

552
00:53:12.032 --> 00:53:16.741
How do you know what's in my closet?
Maybe I have ten dresses like that.

553
00:53:16.829 --> 00:53:19.746
Then they still have
the tags on them,

554
00:53:19.832 --> 00:53:21.492
because I've neve seen you
wear them.

555
00:53:21.584 --> 00:53:23.457
What's with you?

556
00:53:23.544 --> 00:53:26.747
It's just that your things always
come first, your trips, work,

557
00:53:26.964 --> 00:53:28.707
your commitments.

558
00:53:28.799 --> 00:53:32.927
Which is fine, but then don't think
you can tell others what to do.

559
00:53:33.429 --> 00:53:36.549
Do we have to argue over a dress?

560
00:53:36.974 --> 00:53:39.726
Buy it, it looks awful on you,
but if you want...

561
00:53:39.935 --> 00:53:43.269
Again? It's not the dress,
I said you're never around,

562
00:53:43.480 --> 00:53:45.188
your life comes before anything else.

563
00:53:45.274 --> 00:53:48.061
In fact,
I could have stayed home today,

564
00:53:48.152 --> 00:53:51.319
instead I came with you
to buy that fucking dress!

565
00:53:51.405 --> 00:53:52.816
An event!

566
00:53:53.073 --> 00:53:57.023
You don't have a family, kids,
but you never have time!

567
00:53:58.662 --> 00:54:01.497
You have Tommaso, two kids
and always have time for everything,

568
00:54:01.582 --> 00:54:04.073
because you're like a soldier
marching on,

569
00:54:04.168 --> 00:54:06.160
and always judging others.

570
00:54:07.630 --> 00:54:11.793
So, you think since I'm a mother and
a wife, I should dress like a nun?

571
00:54:12.009 --> 00:54:15.342
- So I'm the one who's judging now!
- Listen...

572
00:54:18.724 --> 00:54:21.844
You look terrible in that dress,
but go back and buy it,

573
00:54:22.061 --> 00:54:24.931
you'll feel happier
while cooking this evening. Bye!

574
00:54:26.148 --> 00:54:27.773
Bitch!

575
00:54:28.692 --> 00:54:30.899
Bitch!

576
00:56:07.583 --> 00:56:12.043
Did the hotel personnel
attend to your needs,

577
00:56:12.254 --> 00:56:16.417
without being overbearing
but indulging to your every wish?

578
00:59:31.244 --> 00:59:32.703
Hi.

579
00:59:33.580 --> 00:59:35.537
You're home?

580
00:59:35.748 --> 00:59:38.239
Yes, the rehearsal's postponed
till tomorrow.

581
00:59:38.459 --> 00:59:40.951
Good for you,
I've had a terrible day.

582
00:59:42.297 --> 00:59:45.084
I got a fine and 3 points taken off
my license.

583
00:59:49.012 --> 00:59:50.969
No, the grease-cutter!

584
00:59:52.098 --> 00:59:55.384
- Are you tired?
- Yes, I'm very tired.

585
00:59:56.603 --> 00:59:58.560
Heavens, what's wrong?

586
00:59:58.813 --> 01:00:00.889
You want to leave me.

587
01:00:01.316 --> 01:00:02.774
Are you crazy?

588
01:00:04.444 --> 01:00:07.149
No, of course I don't,

589
01:00:07.363 --> 01:00:09.237
what's the matter?

590
01:00:09.449 --> 01:00:11.525
Come on, darling.

591
01:00:14.579 --> 01:00:16.038
Help me.

592
01:06:32.122 --> 01:06:33.153
Hello?

593
01:06:33.373 --> 01:06:35.282
Silvia, it's me.

594
01:06:35.500 --> 01:06:37.292
What is it?

595
01:06:37.502 --> 01:06:41.915
I'm in Berlin,
but I'll be back in Italy today.

596
01:06:42.174 --> 01:06:44.843
Would you pick me up at the airport?

597
01:06:45.052 --> 01:06:46.925
Please, I really need...

598
01:06:47.137 --> 01:06:48.880
Come pick me up, please, okay?

599
01:06:48.972 --> 01:06:52.471
I can t, I m sorry,
lhave a hell of a week

600
01:06:52.559 --> 01:06:55.975
Take a taxi like always.
I have to go, bye.

601
01:08:29.906 --> 01:08:33.607
They notified her ex-husband,
he hadn't seen her for 15 years,

602
01:08:33.702 --> 01:08:37.534
but he was the only person
who could legally sign those papers.

603
01:08:37.622 --> 01:08:40.243
Suddenly I thought that I also...

604
01:08:40.333 --> 01:08:43.120
Stop it,
it could've happened to anyone.

605
01:08:43.336 --> 01:08:45.910
Let me finish, it's important.

606
01:08:47.757 --> 01:08:50.331
Suddenly I had a tremendous fear

607
01:08:50.552 --> 01:08:53.671
because I've always thought
of myself as free,

608
01:08:54.431 --> 01:08:57.135
living a better life than most others

609
01:08:57.350 --> 01:08:59.426
because they paid me to travel,

610
01:08:59.644 --> 01:09:01.304
to sleep in luxury hotels,

611
01:09:01.396 --> 01:09:05.524
but that's not freedom,
that's loneliness.

612
01:09:07.735 --> 01:09:08.980
No,

613
01:09:09.195 --> 01:09:12.529
that's how you see things now
because you're so upset.

614
01:09:14.451 --> 01:09:16.360
Come here.

615
01:09:22.667 --> 01:09:24.410
I'm scared of losing you,

616
01:09:24.627 --> 01:09:28.672
I'm terrified that the birth
of this child will separate us.

617
01:09:28.756 --> 01:09:30.666
I've said it.

618
01:09:31.718 --> 01:09:35.502
What are you talking about?
I'll always be here for you.

619
01:09:37.182 --> 01:09:39.673
Please, don't leave me.

620
01:09:39.934 --> 01:09:41.345
No.

621
01:10:38.701 --> 01:10:40.361
Sorry.

622
01:10:44.665 --> 01:10:48.414
- What time is it?
- It's 9:30.

623
01:10:48.503 --> 01:10:52.168
Dammit, I'm late,
I have an appointment.

624
01:10:52.256 --> 01:10:55.376
Me too, it's so late,
I have to stop by the house.

625
01:10:56.427 --> 01:10:58.716
- How are you?
- Fine, you?

626
01:10:58.930 --> 01:11:00.590
Wonderful.

627
01:11:01.516 --> 01:11:03.804
- Coffee?
- Yes, please.

628
01:11:03.893 --> 01:11:05.684
Shower?

629
01:11:05.770 --> 01:11:08.225
- You take one first.
- No, you first.

630
01:11:08.314 --> 01:11:10.188
I'll go make coffee.

631
01:11:11.567 --> 01:11:13.643
- A mug?
- Yes.

632
01:11:35.383 --> 01:11:38.965
Is the environment
comfortable and welcoming?

633
01:11:39.220 --> 01:11:41.296
Does it match
your highest expectations?

634
01:11:46.519 --> 01:11:50.517
Do you feel at home, do you perceive
a sense of peace and contentment?

635
01:12:01.450 --> 01:12:05.614
How would you define the unexpected
feeling towards your best friend?

636
01:12:07.957 --> 01:12:11.907
Could it be the solution
to the angst you ve felt lately?

637
01:12:29.854 --> 01:12:31.893
- May I come in?
- Yes.

638
01:12:32.106 --> 01:12:34.597
- Did you forget something?
- No. Are you going out?

639
01:12:34.817 --> 01:12:37.142
No, I was...

640
01:12:37.570 --> 01:12:39.693
Excuse me,

641
01:12:39.780 --> 01:12:43.196
I want to say something important
regarding last night.

642
01:12:43.451 --> 01:12:46.405
Irene, don't worry,
nothing happened last night.

643
01:12:46.495 --> 01:12:48.073
Nothing? You're joking?

644
01:12:48.164 --> 01:12:51.996
No, I mean we can talk
when we have a bit of time.

645
01:12:52.209 --> 01:12:56.124
No, now, or I won't be able
to do anything else, I need...

646
01:12:57.256 --> 01:12:59.877
- How are you?
- Fine.

647
01:12:59.967 --> 01:13:01.592
I'm just fine,

648
01:13:01.677 --> 01:13:05.260
but I had an urgent appointment
to look at another apartment.

649
01:13:05.347 --> 01:13:08.052
I'll make it fast,
I just wanted to say

650
01:13:08.142 --> 01:13:10.929
it was a mistake to make love...

651
01:13:11.020 --> 01:13:13.771
It's my fault, I don't know
what got into me.

652
01:13:14.064 --> 01:13:16.816
I'm leaving,
maybe we can go another time.

653
01:13:17.651 --> 01:13:20.439
No, this is Irene, a friend of mine.

654
01:13:20.529 --> 01:13:22.818
- Yes, we've already met.
- Already met?

655
01:13:23.115 --> 01:13:25.820
- Yes...
- Another time, there's no hurry.

656
01:13:26.035 --> 01:13:29.404
Wait, Fabiana, please don't go!

657
01:13:29.622 --> 01:13:31.614
Everything's wrong today!

658
01:13:32.875 --> 01:13:35.580
Don't hate me, it's an order!

659
01:13:55.064 --> 01:13:57.389
Listen, I don't know
what you know about me,

660
01:13:57.608 --> 01:14:00.609
what Andrea said or,
worse, what you've heard,

661
01:14:00.819 --> 01:14:03.856
but whatever you might have thought
was wrong. - Listen...

662
01:14:03.948 --> 01:14:07.566
Andrea and I were together once,
but it ended a long time ago,

663
01:14:07.701 --> 01:14:11.485
besides, it never worked between us
for reasons I won't get into.

664
01:14:16.752 --> 01:14:20.453
I don't know if you're
really in love with him,

665
01:14:20.547 --> 01:14:24.497
but I'm sure you now
need to feel his presence,

666
01:14:24.593 --> 01:14:28.887
because the baby's on his way,
which is a beautiful thing...

667
01:14:28.973 --> 01:14:30.799
even if it's a little scary.

668
01:14:30.891 --> 01:14:34.723
- Speaking of which, when is it due?
- The end of October.

669
01:14:34.812 --> 01:14:39.770
Andrea is so excited
and he's doing his best...

670
01:14:39.858 --> 01:14:41.436
He is?

671
01:14:42.027 --> 01:14:43.438
Alright,

672
01:14:44.321 --> 01:14:46.693
Andrea and I
were together last night,

673
01:14:46.907 --> 01:14:48.864
but it doesn't mean anything,

674
01:14:49.118 --> 01:14:52.403
I'm sure he's sorry and so am I.

675
01:14:52.496 --> 01:14:56.031
I'm sorry to have barged in
at such a delicate moment,

676
01:14:56.125 --> 01:14:57.619
I apologize.

677
01:14:57.709 --> 01:15:01.790
But, please, go back upstairs,
look at the apartment.

678
01:15:02.423 --> 01:15:04.914
He'll make a wonderful father

679
01:15:05.175 --> 01:15:07.845
and this baby is already very lucky,
you know.

680
01:15:08.053 --> 01:15:10.888
It'll all work out, I promise you.

681
01:15:10.973 --> 01:15:14.092
Don't look at me like that,
you're scaring me.

682
01:15:34.663 --> 01:15:36.739
- Hello.
- Hello.

683
01:15:37.958 --> 01:15:40.034
Who are you looking for?

684
01:15:40.794 --> 01:15:42.336
Silvia Guerrieri.

685
01:15:42.546 --> 01:15:45.915
That's me, this is my house,
but I'm locked out.

686
01:15:48.051 --> 01:15:50.009
I didn't order anything.

687
01:15:50.095 --> 01:15:54.223
It says here, anyway
it's paid in full, just sign.

688
01:15:54.433 --> 01:15:56.342
Hold it for me?

689
01:16:00.480 --> 01:16:02.105
Have a good flight.

690
01:16:35.932 --> 01:16:38.637
- Hello?
- Hi, thanks

691
01:16:40.437 --> 01:16:41.552
Don't mention it.

692
01:16:42.439 --> 01:16:47.017
I'm sorry about the argument,
I should have called to apologize.

693
01:16:47.110 --> 01:16:48.818
Let's drop the whole thing.

694
01:16:49.029 --> 01:16:51.650
You can exchange it
if it's not the right size.

695
01:16:51.740 --> 01:16:54.527
Why don't you come by?
I'll fix you something.

696
01:16:54.743 --> 01:16:58.112
I don't know what, I'm locked out...

697
01:16:58.205 --> 01:17:00.874
Maybe we could go out to eat

698
01:17:00.957 --> 01:17:04.161
I can't, I'm in the airport,
I leave in half an hour.

699
01:17:04.419 --> 01:17:06.211
Where are they sending you?

700
01:17:06.463 --> 01:17:09.666
To Tanzania, but not for work.

701
01:17:10.258 --> 01:17:11.669
A colleague told me

702
01:17:11.885 --> 01:17:14.590
about a small school
in a remote village

703
01:17:14.805 --> 01:17:17.592
where they're looking for a volunteer
to teach children English.

704
01:17:17.682 --> 01:17:20.434
I sent an e-mail, they answered

705
01:17:20.519 --> 01:17:23.270
and I start on Monday.

706
01:17:24.231 --> 01:17:27.018
- What?
- Really,

707
01:17:27.108 --> 01:17:30.643
I thought I'd make
a drastic change in my life

708
01:17:30.862 --> 01:17:33.484
and I want to do it now,
I need to do something useful.

709
01:17:33.698 --> 01:17:37.317
Being in contact with children
will do me good.

710
01:17:37.536 --> 01:17:39.861
Are you crazy?
Tell me you're joking.

711
01:17:40.664 --> 01:17:42.122
Of course I'm joking,

712
01:17:42.332 --> 01:17:45.001
I m going to Shanghai
with my free miles

713
01:17:47.754 --> 01:17:50.459
Is everything alright?

714
01:17:50.674 --> 01:17:52.334
Yes, absolutely.

715
01:17:52.551 --> 01:17:55.255
I'll call you when I get back.

716
01:17:55.345 --> 01:17:57.966
Bye, Silvia, I love you.

717
01:17:58.932 --> 01:18:02.135
I love you too, Irene, bye.

718
01:18:09.818 --> 01:18:13.566
Now that you are about to leave the
place where you ve spent some time,

719
01:18:13.780 --> 01:18:16.983
take a few seconds
to evaluate your experience.

720
01:18:18.118 --> 01:18:21.368
Did it match your expectations?

721
01:18:21.454 --> 01:18:23.032
Would you recommend it to others,

722
01:18:23.123 --> 01:18:28.248
even if you have felt at times
uncomfortable or lonely?

723
01:18:28.336 --> 01:18:30.412
You re still in time
to choose, in the future,

724
01:18:30.630 --> 01:18:32.504
a more comfortable
and protected solution,

725
01:18:32.590 --> 01:18:36.209
maybe more suitable
to the needs of a family

726
01:18:36.302 --> 01:18:39.220
It is well to keep in mind, however,
that happiness and well-being

727
01:18:39.472 --> 01:18:41.548
are strictly personal concepts

728
01:18:41.766 --> 01:18:44.174
For some people the sense
of freedom and adventure

729
01:18:44.269 --> 01:18:47.139
is an essetial part
of the experience.

730
01:18:47.856 --> 01:18:49.848
Trust your instinct,

731
01:18:49.941 --> 01:18:53.440
this is your journey,
the route to take is up to you
